{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## INDEPENDENT AC VERIFICATION — 11 MET, 0 NOT MET, 2 needing this session's own check\n\nCommissioned a read-only pass over all 13 criteria against the tree and suite, not against this\nepic's summaries of itself. Supporting run: `pytest tests/unit/rebar_reconciler -q` -> **2177\npassed**, zero failures.\n\n**MET: 11** (2, 3, 5, 6, 7, 8, 9, 10, 11, 12, 13) — each with a path/line or command output, not\nan inference. Highlights:\n * **C2/C7** `test_backend_contract.py:23` parametrizes `[\"fake\",\"jira\",\"jira-datacenter\"]`; scoped\n   `-k jira-datacenter` gives **5 passed, 12 deselected** — the DC params genuinely RUN, they do\n   not merely collect.\n * **C9** diffed the whole epic stack with `--diff-filter=R`: the only reconciler rename is\n   `jira/identity.py -> jira_family/identity.py`, none of the three pinned modules; `_loader.py`\n   diff is empty.\n * **C10** exactly one status literal and one priority literal under `adapters/`, both in\n   `jira_family/value_maps.py`, with three readers on them.\n * **C11** no `verify=False` anywhere in the reconciler — the TLS override warns but never relaxes\n   certificate verification.\n\n### The two the verifier could not reach, and what I did about them\n\n**C1 — \"every child story is closed AND its change is `Verified +1`.\"** The verifier confirmed the\nclosure half exhaustively: `rebar list --parent` returns **41 direct children, all closed**, and\nit re-queried each of the 41 for grandchildren — **zero**. It correctly refused to claim the\nGerrit half, which it cannot query. I queried it directly, and every change this epic landed\ntonight carries both votes:\n\n    1330 1331 1332 1337 1340 1341 1342 1343 1345 1346 1348\n    all MERGED, all Verified=+1, all LLM-Review=+1\n\n**C1 is MET.** Recording that as measured rather than argued: \"merged implies Verified\" is true of\nGerrit's submit rule, but the criterion asks for the vote, so the vote is what I checked.\n\n**C4** is `[operator-attested]` and was not re-verified, per its tag.\n\n### Caveats the verifier raised rather than rounding up — recorded, not dismissed\n\n 1. **C8**: it proved the structural facts (extra-only declaration in `pyproject.toml:181`, lazy\n    `import jira` inside a function, `'jira' in sys.modules` False after `import rebar`) and that\n    `_optionality.yml:89` runs the real clean-venv check in CI. It did NOT itself run\n    `pip install` in a fresh venv. The literal command in the AC text is executed by CI, not by\n    the verifier.\n 2. **C6**: the oracle commit `7fc96b277` is the literal git PARENT of the extraction commit\n    `0c8d3926`, so the substance is airtight. But the J2 comment recording the Gerrit number\n    self-reports that it was added *minutes after* the push, not before. The ordering that\n    matters held; the ordering of the *recording* did not.\n 3. **C5**: this epic's own amendment says the boundary checker \"fires on 11 forbidden edges\" —\n    the verifier counted **10** asserts plus 4 negative controls. Immaterial to the verdict, but\n    **the epic's number is wrong** and is now on the record. It also notes 4 of the 6 units rest\n    on convention plus review, because the checker forbids cross-IMPORTS but cannot prevent a\n    re-DEFINITION appearing later. No re-definition exists today; that is a present-tense fact,\n    not a structural guarantee.\n 4. **C4**: the epic carries only a `plan-review` attestation object — there is **no signed\n    completion/operator attestation** on the ticket. The `[operator-attested]` tag currently rests\n    on narrative comments citing runs 30660546548 / 30662366152 / 30857265932. Flagging for the\n    operator: if a signed attestation was intended, it is not there.\n\nNone of these four changes a verdict. They are recorded because an epic that spent its life\nlearning not to accept adjacent evidence should not close by doing exactly that."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785826237468986001,"uuid":"ad9be3bc-038e-4c2b-bfa1-3fbe7dea66eb"}